.md
# 24K Gold, Lavender Pearls, and inked custom materials in your 3D plots
Blender, ZBrush, SculptGL, or other programs are the way to go if you want to create sophisticated 3D figures for a presentation, paper, or blog post. However, if you already generate your shapes programmatically or derive them from external data sources, it is convenient to render them using the same set of tools.

WLJS Notebook uses THREE.js on the frontend to render 3D graphics, such as this example:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
# 24K Gold, Lavender Pearls, and inked custom materials in your 3D plots
Blender, ZBrush, SculptGL, or other programs are the way to go if you want to create sophisticated 3D figures for a presentation, paper, or blog post. However, if you already generate your shapes programmatically or derive them from external data sources, it is convenient to render them using the same set of tools.

WLJS Notebook uses THREE.js on the frontend to render 3D graphics, such as this example:

